  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{31}$ and ${a}_{42}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,\u27f6\\,[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form.",
